<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/report.css"><title>VisiSocial</title></head><body><main>
<p class="eyebrow">Research prototype</p><h1>See what your data supports.</h1><p>VisiSocial brings observations from your posts, posting times, page likes and photos into an evidence checklist. Every finding shows its method, source IDs and limitations.</p>
<% if (demo) { %><p class="notice">Offline demonstration. The profile is synthetic. Vision, OpenAI and breach responses are authored mocks. This demonstrates the software; it does not measure the services’ accuracy.</p><form action="/demo" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>"><button>Explore the synthetic profile</button></form><% } else { %><p>Only explicitly allowed Meta developer test users may connect. You choose external processing on the consent screen before an analysis begins.</p><a class="button" href="/auth/facebook">Connect your own test account</a><% } %>
<h2>Evidence first</h2><p>There are no personality scores, composite risk scores or people searches. AI guesses remain guesses. Small samples produce “insufficient evidence”.</p><h2>Privacy</h2><p>Local records expire after 24 hours. You can delete your record sooner. Third-party retention and downloaded copies are outside local deletion.</p>
</main></body></html>
